ing all  might is thinking about deku about how  he made a promise to encode that he  would protect deku and yet deku decided  to go off on his own and leave all might  behind i mean he even left that freaking  bento box which was not cool and then  deku almost got himself killed before  his classmates came to his rescue and of  course all might feels terrible because  he wasn't there to help him this is  something that weighs heavily on all  might's shoulders especially since he  knows that even if he was there he  probably wouldn't have been able to do  much against the villain in his current  physical state the small might form as  we call it there isn't much that all  might can do even if he wanted to  eventually all might finds himself in  that same square where deku had faced  the villain dictator and then after that  his own classmates all might sees deku's  disheveled mask on the ground and so he  picks up the mask and looks upon the  large statue of all might that is  located in the square the statue that  now has a sign over it that reads i am  not here almight again thinks about the  fact that he couldn't even protect his  own student deku and he says to the  statue and also to himself that he  almight is just dragging everyone down  this is again where those unrealistic  standards that i mentioned many times  before come into play in the past  almight was the symbol of peace the  symbol of the hero society itself as  long as all might was around everyone  was fine because they knew that this  incredibly strong hero was always  watching and he would do anything to  protect the people all might had set  such an insanely high standard for  heroes that people started relying on  them too much they relied on heroes to  solve all of their problems heroes  became celebrities and many of the  heroes became more interested in money  and fame than actual heroics after all  if all might is always there to save the  day when things get really bad then do  other heroes really need to worry about  the danger and sacrifice aspect of being  a hero all might will take care of all  the real problems while other lesser  known heroes can just focus on money and  fame obviously this was not the mindset  of every hero but as we saw in the  previous arc many heroes were fair  weather heroes and when things got bad  they bailed once all might could no  longer live up to those impossible  standards that he himself had set the  hero society collapsed pretty quickly  and all might is now left wondering  whether he is partially to blame for all  of it but almight's train of thought is  soon interrupted by a sword-wielding  maniac who holds a blade up to his face  that maniac is none other than the hero  killer stain and it seems that he heard  toshinori's previous comment about all  might dragging people down this comment  straight up triggered stain and with a  crazy look in his eyes he demands that  this skinny blonde man in front of him  take back what he said about all might  stain of course doesn't realize that he  is speaking to all might himself or at  least that's what stain wants us to  believe as i said toshinoriagi is  currently in his small mite form and  this is a form that stain doesn't  necessarily recognize stain seems to  think that this man is just some random  dude insulting the greatest hero of all  time and he refuses to stand by and  allow that to happen toshinori explains  that a lot has changed since stain had  gone to prison and he reveals that he is  in fact almight stain is shocked by this  and he refuses to believe it at first  but toshinori demonstrates that he is  almight by briefly transforming back  into his talmide form and yet stain  still refuses to believe that this thin  frail man is the larger than life hero  whom he respects so much stain proclaims  that this square where all might statue  stands is sacred ground built to honor  true heroes so how dare this weak fake  try to impersonate the greatest hero and  toshinori actually agrees that he is a  fake in a way he spent his entire life  trying to make a difference and trying  to help those who were powerless but in  the end he himself ended up powerless he  couldn't even protect his own student  despite making a promise to his mother  not to mention the fact that he couldn't  stop the collapse of the entire hero  society all might laments the fact that  he keeps getting further and further  away from the hero he once was but stain  refuses to listen stain seems to be on  the verge of having a mental breakdown  just listening to all might sounding so  hopeless and defeated and this kind of  reminds me of deku deku would probably  be just as shocked as staying if he  heard his idol talking this way which is  interesting in a way deku and stain are  two very different people and yet they  do share some similar ideals and at the  end of the day they are both all might  fanboys stain then grabs almight but he  doesn't grab him in a violent or  threatening way he grabs him in order to  show him a lone woman walking up to the  almighty statue the woman uses her quirk  to climb the statue and take down the  sign which says i am not here stain  explains that every single day this  woman comes here to clean the statue  from any vandalism conducted by the  anti-hero protesters even though this is  a dangerous task this area is not safe  anymore and those who keep vandalizing  the statue could attack her at any  moment the woman still risks her life  every day to defend the legacy of all  might toshinori is surprised by this he  doesn't know why this woman would bother  risking her life for some statue but  stane explains that she is the last  person all might had saved back during  the kamino incident she had been stuck  under some rubble and she would have  died if all might hadn't defeated all  for one in time for her to be rescued as  toshinori looks on in stunned silence  stain goes into a crazed rant about how  all might always kept a smile on his  face and always protected the people  this had nothing to do with his quirk  the man known as almight had unwavering  determination and dedicated his entire  life to preserve peace stain says that  as he is now toshinori can't even hold a  candle to all might but it's not over  yet that woman who cleans the statue  every day is proof that the cinders  which all might left behind continued to  burn within those who followed in his  footsteps these cinders are now forming  into a great fire as all of class 1a  unites under the same banner that all  might had once raised and that flame  must not be allowed to die they must  stoke it no matter how difficult the  situation becomes this speech is  actually pretty nuts when you think  about it the crazed villain known as  stain a man who has murdered dozens of  heroes is basically giving almight a pep  talk and reminding him that deku and  class 1a are now carrying the torch that  he had passed to them stain the hero  killer is praising the virtues of the  heroes and telling all might not to give  up this is not the kind of conversation  that toshita was expecting to have today  or any other day as he continues to look  at that woman who is cleaning the statue  toshinori sheds a tear stain turns to  walk away and as he leaves he tells  toshinori that a hero exists for the  sake of others and while he still  doesn't want to admit that this man is  really almight he tells him that if he  is a true hero then he will use the  information that stain had gathered from  tartarus we then see that stain left a  piece of paper on the ground a piece of  paper that he wants toshinori to read  stain then invites all might to one day  come and end him the villain who had  murdered 40 heroes it's almost like  stain is trying to encourage almight by  saying that once the villain crisis is  over and japan is saved he can come and  settle the score with him as well the  final words that come out of stain's  mouth are everything is for the sake of  a just society and as the rain finally  stops all might tears continue to flow  down his cheeks and that is how the  chapter ends wow what an unexpected  emotional moment a depressed and  powerless almighty getting a  motivational speech from a villain who  killed dozens of heroes and no matter  what you think of stain the man was  spitting and the interesting thing about  staying here is that he seems to be  partially in denial that his hero  almighty is now this weak and sad man  known as toshinoriagi and yet another  part of staying clearly knows that this  is almight if he didn't believe that  this was him what would be the point of  that motivational speech what would be  the point of leaving this random man  that note stain knows that this is all  might even if he doesn't want to admit  it and that makes this whole situation  even more emotional and impactful stain  wants toshinori to keep struggling and  pushing forward so that he can once  again live up to the legacy of all might  and then we have that note as of the end  of the chapter we have no idea what the  note says all we know is that stain got  some valuable information from tartarus  and that he wants the heroes to have it  but what could that information be is it  about a traitor who made the prison  break possible is it about the prisoners  who escaped and their quirks is it  something else entirely man stain is  such a fascinating characters and one of  my favorite characters in the entire  story i loved seeing this confrontation  and i really hope that we get to see  more of staying because he is just so  interesting i mean he's clearly not a  good person and clearly he does horrible  things and yet he does have some ideals  that we can totally relate to and he  even shares some of the same ideals as  our heroes deku and all might obviously  stain also has other warped ideals that  the heroes don't share but still it's so  interesting to think about stain's 